Subject: [PATCH] fonts: preserve design-space paths for Mac profiles

FreeType rounds outline points at SkFont's 64px canonical path size before
Skia rescales them. For byte-identical Songti, this predicts every measured
18/40px bound error. Select design-space extraction with an immutable SkFont
flag supplied only by Blink's existing Mac-profile loader; no Profile in Skia.

The flag participates in SkFont identity/serialization and full scaler records
used by strike/path caches. Flagged unhinted scalable paths load at units_per_EM
size without NO_SCALE or NO_RECURSE. Keep the actual variation/composite loader,
restore size/transform, and use Skia's float transform after decomposition.
Synthetic bold, tricky fonts and color/SVG/sbix faces retain the original
path and operation order, including hybrid faces with monochrome outlines. Advance precision and the missing PingFang HVF provider are separate.

Reference: resources/fingerprints/raw/m4-max-chrome-20260908T163229Z.json and
same-version native/candidate named-face diagnostics. Candidate requires
integrated Skia V1, cache tests and native multi-size comparisons before V3.

This patch deliberately does not carry the upstream change's own test update
to third_party/skia/tests/FontTest.cpp, which extended the flag-coverage loop
to the new kDesignSpacePaths bit. That file is in skia's test_lib("tests"),
inside `if (skia_enable_tools)`, and skia.gni defines skia_enable_tools =
is_skia_dev_build = is_skia_standalone && !is_official_build. Every target in
build/args sets is_official_build = true, so no configuration this repository
produces compiles it -- confirmed absent from the macos-arm64 ninja graph. A
hunk nothing compiles can never be verified at any tier, and it is additive
coverage rather than a compile fix: the four files that do build compile
without it. The upstream test exists if anyone rebases against a dev build.

diff --git a/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/fonts/font_platform_data.cc b/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/fonts/font_platform_data.cc
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/fonts/font_platform_data.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/fonts/font_platform_data.cc
@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@
 
 #include "third_party/blink/renderer/platform/fonts/font_platform_data.h"
 
+#include "base/apostate/profile.h"
 #include "base/compiler_specific.h"
 #include "base/feature_list.h"
 #include "build/build_config.h"
@@ -264,6 +265,10 @@
 #if !BUILDFLAG(IS_MAC) && !BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN) && !BUILDFLAG(IS_IOS)
 SkFont FontPlatformData::CreateSkFont(const FontDescription*) const {
   SkFont font(typeface_);
+  if (const auto* profile = base::apostate::Profile::Get();
+      profile && profile->ua_platform() && *profile->ua_platform() == "macOS") {
+    font.setDesignSpacePaths(true);
+  }
   style_.ApplyToSkFont(&font);
 
   const float ts = text_size_ >= 0 ? text_size_ : 12;
